==Strategy==
Welcome to Youcan hell, where endless torrents of powerful [[Wave Attack]]s shred everything they touch. Anything vulnerable to Waves can and will be destroyed in seconds, so unless ranged Wave Shields are in play, they don't stand a chance. Youcan's extremely durable 266,000 HP Barrier is also concerning despite his low health, meaning the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] is absolutely necessary, as most [[Barrier Breaker]]s cannot hope to reach and attack Youcan in the first place, let alone destroy his Barrier.

The goal of this stage is to outlast the onslaught by holding off the Youcans and Sleipnir until the former stops spawning.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] - Being able to outrange Youcan with [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] and [[Massive Damage]] to Angels, with proper meatshielding Mushroom can delete Youcans as well as Gabriels quickly.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - Despite there being no Traitless threats in this stage, Hitman's Wave Immunity makes it a serviceable [[Long Distance]] midranger.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] - Dancer's Wave Immunity makes it another supplementary midranger who can provide consistent damage.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - Most threats here are Angels, so despite its vulnerability to Waves Ramen can still tank massive amounts of damage from the nasty angels and prevent them from pushing, especially when aided with Research [[Cat Combo]]s.
*Talented [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Acrobat Cats]]: A spammable, Waveproof crowd-controller that can use [[Surge Attack]]s to knockback both the Youcan hordes and Angelic Sleipnir.
*[[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]] - Despite Musashi's horrendous stats, he is one of the few Wave Immune backliners available, so unless other alternatives can be procured, he might be needed to provide some DPS.
*[[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Costumed Witchy Neneko]] - This rare, seasonal cat outranges Youcan with the [[Wave Shield]] ability, allowing non-Wave Immune units to last a long time on the field. It cannot outrange Sleipnir, however, so killing it prior to breaking any barriers is recommended, otherwise she may be prematurely killed or knocked back as Wave Attacks kill your units. Long Distance units such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] and [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] can be used to great effect with Witchy Neneko, where they would struggle otherwise.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any Wave Immune Uber that outranges Angelic Sleipnir is very much welcomed here.
*[[Gunduros (Uber Rare Cat)|Ballistic Dragon Gunduros]] - With enough frontline protection, Gunduros' immense range and [[Massive Damage]] against Aliens will prove perfect for this stage, alongside its Wave Immunity, being able to easily nuke the fair amount of Youcans in this stage, even when they stack together, while also clearing the Celeboodles. It can also provide great damage against Sleipnir, although it cannot Knockback or Slow him, so be careful if you plan to use this unit here.

==Trivia==
*Banana Genomes could be a throwback to [[Haunted Genome]], which also spams [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] ([[UltraBaaBaa]]) with 266k-HP [[Barrier]]s.

